   "design": "Quantities come from the mine plan export, unit rates for standard items from the price table, and a reader proposes rates from supplier quotes with the page for each, checked against quote totals. Actual metres, tonnes and hours from the production system's shift records load into the schedule, instead of being typed from shift reports. The cost and schedule report takes its estimate and schedule tables from the estimate and the schedule. Scheduling, estimating, benchmark checks, the report text, discussions and supplier mail stay with the engineer.",
   "previous_blocker": "Quantities, rates and actuals were typed by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Plan exports, price tables, quote reading and production records.",
   "still_hard": "Rates for new equipment.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which estimate line is optimistic.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less typing; estimating judgement stays.",
